    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_8a42ccf96bb35aec3fd75fdf8a1bf2ef0e29f9238be5bc9f3abca494e207e8e8",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Modified Mellin convolution gives a recursive calculus for moment transforms: a product of lower moments yields Z_{k+l} as a contour convolution of Z_k and Z_l, while smooth localized inversion couples their spectral frequencies; for k=l=2 this connects Z2 information to the eighth moment and motivates, only heuristically, the square-root scale proposed for the spectral exponential sum.",
