    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_a86f3fd1ab3fe797f16585031d69e23f6526347651e38042a47161ed83bf2328",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Modified Mellin inversion, localization, and Parseval connect three kinds of control without making them equivalent: bounds for the fourth-moment error E2 feed mean-square estimates for Z2, sufficiently strong Z2 mean-square estimates recover E2 control, and conjectural Z2 control yields strong eighth- and other zeta-moment bounds after smoothing and polar subtraction.",
